<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Claudia Sheinbaum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Claudia Sheinbaum is a Mexican scientist and politician who became the first woman president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> on 1 October 2024. Trained as an energy engineer, she served as environment secretary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-manuel-lopez-obrador">Andrés Manuel López Obrador</a> and then as head of government of the capital from 2018 to 2023. She won the 2024 election by a large margin as candidate of the Morena party, promising to continue López Obrador's programme.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/claudia-sheinbaum.jpg" alt="Claudia Sheinbaum" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eneas · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Claudia_Sheinbaum_in_2025_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
